.TH CASCADE 1 "October 2026" "cascade 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cascade, cascade-gtk, cascaded \- BitTorrent client with a GTK app, a command line and a web interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cascade
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR [\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPW\fR]] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B cascade-gtk
[\fITORRENT\fR...]
.br
.B cascaded
[\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cascade is a BitTorrent client built on libtorrent.  One background service,
.BR cascaded ,
owns all torrents and settings.  The GTK app
.RB ( cascade-gtk ),
the command line
.RB ( cascade )
and the optional web interface are clients of that service, so all three always show the same torrents and the
same settings.  The GTK app starts the service when needed; it keeps running after the window closes unless
"Keep running in the background" is turned off.
.PP
Torrents are named by their number in
.BR "cascade list" ,
a unique prefix (4 or more characters) of their info hash, or a unique part of their name.
Most commands accept several torrents, or
.BR all .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list ", " ls " [\fB\-f\fR \fIFILTER\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISORT\fR] [\fISEARCH\fR]"
List torrents.  Filters: all, downloading, seeding, completed, paused, queued, active, checking, error.
.TP
.BR watch ", " top
A live view of the list (Ctrl+C quits).
.TP
.B status
Speeds, listening port, bound interface, slow mode, schedule and web interface.
.TP
.BI add " SOURCE..." " \fR[\fB\-p\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILABEL\fR] [\fB\-\-paused\fR] [\fB\-\-sequential\fR] [\fB\-\-first\-last\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR]"
Add magnet links, .torrent files or URLs of .torrent files.
.TP
.BI info " T" ", files " T " [\-\-set N=PRIO...], peers " T " [\-\-add IP:PORT], trackers " T " [\-\-add URL] [\-\-remove URL]"
Details of one torrent.  File priorities are skip, low, normal or high (0\-7); ranges such as 1\-5=high work.
.TP
.BI pause ", " resume ", " start ", " recheck ", " reannounce " T..."
Pause, resume, force-start (skip the queue), verify the data, or ask the trackers for peers now.
.TP
.BI remove " T... " "\fR[\fB\-\-data\fR] [\fB\-y\fR]"
Remove torrents, optionally with their downloaded files.
.TP
.BI move " T... DIR" ", queue " "T... up|down|top|bottom"
Move the data, or move torrents in the queue.
.TP
.BI limit " T... " "\fR[\fB\-\-down\fR \fIKIB\fR] [\fB\-\-up\fR \fIKIB\fR] [\fB\-\-connections\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-slots\fR \fIN\fR]"
Per-torrent limits (0 = default).
.TP
.BI option " T... " "\-\-set KEY=VALUE..."
Per-torrent options: sequential, first_last, super_seeding, auto_managed, ratio_limit, seed_time_limit, label.
.TP
.BI label " T... " "\-\-to LABEL" ", labels " "[\-\-add NAME [\-\-path DIR]] [\-\-remove NAME]"
Set labels, list them, or create a label with its own download folder.
.TP
.BI magnet " T" ", export " "T [\-o FILE]"
Print the magnet link, or save the .torrent file.
.TP
.BR slow " [on|off|toggle]"
Slow mode: the alternative speed limits.  A manual change lasts until the schedule next changes.
.TP
.BR schedule " [show | on | off | clear | set \fIDAYS HOURS MODE\fR]"
The weekly schedule.  DAYS: mon\-fri, weekend, sat,sun, all.  HOURS: 9\-17, 22\-6, all.  MODE: normal, slow, pause.
.TP
.BR config " [\fIPAGE\fR|\fIKEY\fR], " get " \fIKEY\fR..., " set " \fIKEY VALUE\fR..., " reset
Show and change settings.  Every setting of the preferences window has a key (see
.BR "cascade config" ).
.TP
.BR port " [random]"
Show the listening port, or pick a new random one.
.TP
.B interfaces
Network interfaces to bind to (net.interface), with their addresses.
.TP
.BR webui " [status | on | off | password [\fIPW\fR] | open]"
The web interface.  Turning it on without a password creates one and prints it.
.TP
.BI create " PATH " "\fR[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fITRACKER\fR]... [\fB\-\-private\fR] [\fB\-\-v1\fR|\fB\-\-v2\fR] [\fB\-\-seed\fR]"
Create a .torrent file (hybrid v1+v2 by default).
.TP
.BR boot " [status | enable | disable] [\fB\-\-user\fR \fINAME\fR]"
Start the service when the computer starts, before anyone logs in: a systemd user unit with lingering (no root
needed), or, as root (it uses sudo or doas by itself), a runit service, an OpenRC service, or a FreeBSD or OpenBSD
rc.d script that runs as the user.
.TP
.BR blocklist ", " log " [\-n N], " daemon " [\-\-detach], " stop ", " gui
Reload the IP blocklist, show the service log, run or stop the service, open the GTK app.
.SH NETWORK
.TP
.B Interface binding and kill switch
.B cascade set net.interface tun0
sends all traffic through one device.  With net.killswitch on (the default) every transfer pauses while the
device is down or has no address, so nothing goes over the normal connection.
.TP
.B Port modes
net.port_mode is fixed, random (a new port at every start, between net.random_min and net.random_max),
natpmp (VPN port forwarding: the port is requested from net.natpmp_gateway every 45 seconds, e.g. 10.2.0.1 for
ProtonVPN) or file (read from net.port_file, e.g. gluetun's /tmp/gluetun/forwarded_port).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CASCADE_URL, CASCADE_PASSWORD
Use a remote Cascade web interface instead of the local service.
.TP
.B CASCADE_HOME
Keep configuration, data, logs and the socket under one directory.
.TP
.B CASCADE_CONFIG_DIR, CASCADE_DATA_DIR, CASCADE_STATE_DIR, CASCADE_RUN_DIR, CASCADE_SOCKET
Override single locations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cascade/settings.json
Settings (written by the service only).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cascade/
Torrents (resume data), labels and statistics.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/cascade/cascade.log
The log.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cascade/cascade.sock
The control socket (only your user can open it).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cascade add 'magnet:?xt=urn:btih:...' -l linux
cascade list -f downloading
cascade files 2 --set 3=skip 1=high
cascade set net.interface wg0
cascade set net.port_mode natpmp
cascade schedule set mon-fri 9-17 slow
cascade webui on
CASCADE_URL=http://nas:8150 cascade status
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/Smiley-McSmiles/Cascade-GTK
.UE
